==Description==
The '''Korblox Soul''' was an enemy that appears in [[The Hunt: Mega Edition Event]]. It also appears in [[The Classic Event]] missions as part of [[Sandbox Mode|Sandbox]] mode. It has a decent amount of health and a slightly fast speed. Additionally, it is a [[Hidden (Attribute)|Hidden]] enemy, meaning only towers with hidden detection can target it.

==Logbook Description==
"''Korblox Souls are Serveabelum's slaves who perished while working in the Bubbling Pits. The chains they carry are remnants of the shackles that bound them in life, and the helmets they wear come from the ruins of the White Blind fortress. Even in death, they will serve The Korblox Empire.''"

==Appearance==
The '''Korblox Soul''' has blue skin. It does not have a head, torso or legs, though it does have a rib cage. It wears a grey helmet, grey cloth around waist and has chains wrapped around its arms. It also has multiple blue spikes on its shoulders.

==Strategy==
As this enemy only appears through [[Sandbox Mode|Sandbox]] mode, no strategy section is made for its current version. Instead, a strategy section for the one that appeared without [[Sandbox Mode|Sandbox]] mode in [[Korblox Temple]] is listed instead.
*Early-game towers with hidden detection, like the [[Militant]], [[Rocketeer]], [[Medic]] or [[Brawler]] can be useful against this.
**Towers which can easily damage them indirectly, such as the [[Trapper]], can also be used.
**As [[Korblox Temple]] gives a large amount of cash, towers like the [[Ace Pilot]] or [[Firework Technician]] can be used to give your towers hidden detection.
*High DPS towers with hidden detection, like the [[Minigunner]], [[Turret]], [[Accelerator]] or [[Engineer]] can be used against this.

